Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Remote Preflight Private Permit Bridge P0 Data Design

@ [data_design_uuid] 42fd995a-65df-4871-a667-0bb8c1fc466b
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] 750fbbb5-f72f-4816-882f-d8b0ebf1acc7

& [OpaqueAdmission]
  + crate-private type with private fields request_sha256 proposal_sha256 proposal_verification_sha256 decision_sha256 correspondence_sha256 producer_plan_sha256 observed_time_ms activation_implementation_commit activation_bookend runner_implementation_commit runner_bookend permit_limit1 runner_limit1 process_limit1 retry_count0 fixture_only false
  + no Clone Copy Default Serialize Deserialize public fields public constructor or machine form
  + a consuming private coordinate extractor permits the runner issuer to validate but cannot duplicate the admission

& [RunnerPermitIssuer]
  + exactly one crate-private function in the runner module accepts the admission and producer plan by value and reference respectively
  + it checks every fixed lineage ceiling fixture and producer-plan coordinate before constructing the existing three-private-field permit
  + permit fields and existing validate_permit runner entry contained backend receipt and public validation semantics remain unchanged

& [BridgeCore]
  + private generic core accepts one admission all exact typed inputs and one FnOnce runner function
  + all activation and producer inputs are revalidated before issuance
  + admission is moved into issuance and the returned permit is moved immediately into the FnOnce runner call
  + no admission or permit appears in any return error log debug serialization or terminal value

& [TerminalOutcome]
  + crate-private nonserializable nonclone type with private disposition permit_consumed runner_invocations optional validated run and exact effect-account fields
  + dispositions completed_available completed_provider_unavailable abandoned_after_consumption and receipt_refused
  + successful runs pass to-machine-form from-machine-form and validate operations before completion; any mismatch becomes receipt_refused
  + all outcomes after issuance carry permit_consumed true runner_invocations1 and no outgoing transition

& [ProviderFreeTests]
  + descendant unit tests construct private fixture admission literals and supply one FnOnce mock closure without adding a test constructor symbol
  + synthetic run bytes originate from existing provider-free fixtures and no production bridge entry process backend or remote host is invoked
